My XL14 ranger went down last night. The second centaur with
a /oDeath on the quest was one too many. I started to label
this YAAD, but there were ways that this sad ending could
have been avoided, I just don't know if a prudent player
would have chosen them.

This ranger had two glaring weaknesses, no reflection and no
MR. A secondary concern was no ability to blind herself,
mostly an inconvenience since she had a ring of warning and
an amulet of ESP. She had some really good things going,
intrinsic teleport and TC, a =oPC and a !oPoly, displaced
and invisible, very fast and unburdened.

She had exhausted her create monster stuff at the various
altars, opened every container in the dungeon thus far and
even dug up a few graves when !oOD showed something inside.
Other than wandering aimlessly, the choices seemed to be
Medusa's Titan and then dig through, Levelport below Medusa
and head for the castle, Ludios or the quest. Of the four,
the castle and the quest seemed best since success would
solve at least one of the problems.

I chose the quest since I judged that, while offering less
reward, I was less likely to meet liches there. The end was
frustrating, on Home 1, a centaur fired off a /oDeath which
missed, a /oSleep allowed my ranger to confiscate the first
/oDeath. On Home 3 it happened again, only this time it
didn't miss. It seems with AC -21, invisible and displaced,
the odds of missing were pretty good.

It could have been avoided. I could have used the =oPC and
the !oPoly to become a master lich, vampire lord, gray or
silver dragon. I could have routinely worn the =oPC so when
I hit that poly trap on Home 2, I could have chosen a useful
form instead of spending time as a killer bee. I didn't,
just in case I ran into something firing lightning at me.

In retrospect, another choice was to walk back up through
the dungeon quaffing every fountain above Level 20, there
were several.

I think perhaps the best choice would have been to levelport
to -50, I assume I would end up in the VotD near the stairs
or in front of the castle, In either case, use the =oPC and
the !oPoly to become a Xorn, that and the =oLevitation
should've let me get to the wand before fighting the hordes.

What do you think, YAAD or YASD.

